Z||000000||JBGehling||11-26-2000||11:29 AM||||Does anyone know where to find a COMPLETE kit to convert an 88 GT automatic, to a five-speed? <BR>JOsh||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-26-2000||01:00 PM||||there is no such thing. you can try <BR><A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com/" TARGET=_blank>Kick Hill Farm</A>. he at least has all the parts you need.<P>In addition to the obvious you must install the correct MEMCAL/PROM in the ECM for a stick.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||11-26-2000||01:07 PM||||I changed my 88 Mera from an automatic to a Getrag 5 speed. I bought the stuff from Bob Parker (Fiero Hill). I told him I did the Mera Registry and sent him a sales flyer showing all the Fiero stuff I sold at that time. I told him my 88 Mera had 29,000 miles on it and it in pristene condition. Most of what he sent was good quality. But the Getrag trans. he sent was beyond junk. When I called he said he sent a good one with 20,000 miles on it. I hung up in disgust. I could not believe it. Of all the people to rip off he rips me off. I wonder about that guy. I will never buy anything from him again and I never send any business his way. Bad choice on his part. The up side is I bought a FWD Beretta Getrag and developed the FWD conversion kit. I have sold well over 100 of these kits helping many Fiero owners use the FWD Getrags in Fieros! ||||reg||1
